@lucasliao0403 — I re-reviewed unchanged head `4e123050ee6ff2a8c86ccf678735380ad87eea6f`. The five corrected sites now use the port owner's TP size, consistently with the existing dial/read paths; I found no technical issue preventing review within the SMG scope below.

Follow-up to [our earlier validation](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/64574#issuecomment-6553580710): we have since tested the **official PyPI SMG 1.13.0 wheel**, rather than only the private CI binary:

- **52087, two MI355X nodes, WRITE/RDMA:** Qwen3-30B-A3B bf16, P DP2/TP1/EP2 → D DP2/TP2/EP4. Four serial same-rank/direct-reference checks and eight requests at concurrency 4 passed; 37,772 routed prompt tokens were external KV, with D local compute/cache = 0. Five isolated NIC windows (excluding reference requests) exactly matched the full padded KV payload: **3,722,969,088 bytes**.
- **52089, one MI355X node, WRITE/XGMI:** P DP2/TP2/EP4 → D DP2/TP1/EP2, same model revision. The actual [SMG regression (now Ready for review)](https://github.com/smg-project/smg/pull/4780) passed: **1 passed in 279.98s**, with four serial and eight concurrent checks, 38,828 external-KV prompt tokens and D local compute/cache = 0. This case retains metric deltas, not original before/after snapshots, and makes no RDMA-byte claim.

[Public configuration/results](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/59116#issuecomment-6560545424). Both runs cleanly backported this head's unchanged three-file production diff onto ROCm7.2/df6603 (including #61726); they did not test the whole PR-head tree or a pristine image. Declared Cairo/name-data repairs and the RDMA-only provider repair remain as disclosed; 36 serving-native and 12 engine-metadata identities stayed fixed. The identical upstream test file also passed all 30 cases in each of these three containers (90 executions). These are owned runs, not hosted-CI results.

This supports **equal DP2, one pod per role, sequential WRITE** in the two stated TP directions; it does not establish other models/modes, unequal DP, multi-pod release, small-P→large-D XGMI or failure reclamation. Are there remaining author-side Draft tasks we can help with? If not, I recommend marking this Ready for review based on this scoped review and validation.

